    "subtopic": "Text structure and purpose",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "passage": "The following text is from Ameen Rihani’s 1921 poem “The Wanderer.”\n I wander among the hills of alien lands Where Nature her prerogative resigns To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines And all the arts and sciences commands.\n<u>But in my soul The eastern billows roll—\nI hear the voices of my native strands.</u>",
